    <string name="sp_help_couplers_strength">Overall multiplier on the DIR coupler inhibition; 1 is the film default.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_date">Exposes a date-back imprint onto the negative, so the digits develop, glow and grain with the picture instead of being pasted on top.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_date_ev">How strongly the LED exposes the film, in stops above mid-grey; brighter digits bloom more.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_date_size">Digit height, with the Android default as 1×.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_dev_contrast">Gamma factor of the negative density curves: above 1 is more contrast, below 1 flatter.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_di">Digital Intermediate reads the negative in printing density and writes it as Cineon Log, viewed through the DI view, bypassing the paper print. Negative films only; Scan film directly takes precedence.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_diffusion_spread">Changes the halo width without changing its strength. 1× keeps the selected filter\'s modeled size.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_diffusion_strength">The filter grade (as in commercial 1/8, 1/4, 1/2, 1, 2 grades).</string>
    <string name="sp_help_dir">DIR couplers inhibit neighbouring layers during development, shaping colour separation and edges. Not used by monochrome models.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_enlarger_diffusion">Simulates diffusion in the enlarger light path before the paper is exposed. Separate from print/scan glare.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_enlarger_exposure">Changes the virtual enlarger\'s exposure, in stops: right prints lighter, left darker.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_exposure_comp">Adds a bias to the auto-exposure, in EV (stops). Right is brighter, left darker.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_film_format">The physical film format. It sets the real-millimetre scale at which grain and halation act on the picture: a smaller format makes grain relatively more visible.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_filter_m">Enlarger magenta filter shift from neutral, in Kodak CC units.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_filter_y">Enlarger yellow filter shift from neutral, in Kodak CC units.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_glare_strength">A multiplier on the glare light; 1× is the engine default.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_grain">Turns the film grain simulation on.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_grain_size">Changes the modeled particle diameter relative to 1×. Film format still sets its physical scale; this does not alter the stock profile.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_grain_softness">Smooths the grained density image, separately from particle size. 1× preserves the original softness; 0× disables this smoothing. Fine image texture can also soften.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_halation">Light reflected back into the emulsion by the film base, the source of halation. Follow film uses the selected film\'s own anti-halation layer; High, Medium and Low set a layer that lets through more or less halation; Off switches the stage out of the render.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_halation_strength">A multiplier on the chosen halation setting: 1× leaves it as chosen, up to 4× amplifies the reflection.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_headroom">Estimates light lost in clipped highlights before film exposure. 0 EV uses the recorded light; applies to CineStill\'s default back-reflection model. Argentroom feathers the boosted area\'s edge (not upstream behaviour) so a phone JPEG\'s hard clip does not leave a step.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_highlight_expansion">Expands compressed highlight detail in the completed paper image, using the paper\'s measured tone map. Not available when the print is bypassed or on a black-and-white paper.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_hint">Long-press a name or tap ⓘ for help</string>
    <string name="sp_help_lens_diffusion">Simulates a diffusion filter in front of the camera lens, before film exposure. Separate from film halation.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_metering">Film auto-exposure sets the exposure baseline: Balanced, Center, Protect highlights, Protect shadows and Center weighted weigh the frame differently; Off uses only the compensation below.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_paper_contrast">Reshapes the selected paper\'s density response, separate from film development contrast. 1× preserves the original paper profile.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_paper_glare">Glare from viewing or digitising the finished paper image; separate from film halation and enlarger diffusion.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_paper_grade">Multigrade filtration on the enlarger: 00 is softest, 5 hardest. Mid-grey stays put while contrast changes.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_preflash">A faint, even exposure of the paper before the real one; opens the deepest shadows and lowers contrast slightly, leaving highlights largely alone.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_print_effects">The switch for paper pre-flash and paper glare.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_scan_direct">Shows the scanned film directly instead of a print — natural for reversal (positive) film. A negative shows as the raw orange negative.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_scan_sharpen">Unsharp masking at the scan. Strength is a multiplier; 1× is the default.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_scatter">Overall light scatter inside the emulsion; 1 is the full physical scatter.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_sublayers">Sub-layer grain model: each emulsion layer grains separately. Not used by monochrome films.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_temperature">Colour temperature in kelvin for a custom white balance.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_tint">Green/magenta tint for a custom white balance; 0 is neutral. Android converts it to a LibRaw green multiplier, not yet calibrated value-for-value against iOS.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_unavailable">Silverphase iOS has this parameter but the Android engine has no matching stage yet, so it keeps its place and stays disabled rather than faking a look-alike.</string>
    <string name="sp_help_wb_preset">The RAW capture white balance. Daylight, Tungsten etc. are fixed presets; Custom uses the temperature and tint below.</string>
